# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECURITY FIX (2026-11-07). This file did not exist, which means `docker build`
# sent the ENTIRE working tree into the build context — including:
#   .env                  → DATABASE_URL and any future secrets
#   .z-ai-config          → the live model-gateway API key
#   prisma/db/custom.db   → EVERY NOVEL THE USER HAS WRITTEN
#   node_modules/         → ~800 MB of pointless upload per build
# `next build` copies .env files into .next/standalone, so the database file and
# credentials would have been baked into the published image.
#
# Rule: the image must contain CODE ONLY. Data and credentials are injected at
# runtime (volume mount + environment / secret manager).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- credentials & local config -------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.z-ai-config
*.pem

# --- LIVE DATABASE: never bake user novels into an image --------------------
prisma/db/
db/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# --- dependencies (installed inside the image) ------------------------------
node_modules

# --- build outputs (produced inside the image) ------------------------------
.next
out
build
coverage

# --- local artifacts, logs, scratch -----------------------------------------
*.log
dev.log
dev.out.log
server.log
*-tmp.ts
tool-results/
upload/
*.pid

# --- version control & editor/agent state -----------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.vercel
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode

# --- docs & design notes (not needed at runtime) ----------------------------
agent-ctx
*.md
!README.md

# --- this file & deployment scripts (the VM runs them, the image doesn't) ----
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
deploy/
